# Cha's virtual gamepads belong to environments, not to this machine.
#
# cha-streamer creates them in two ways, and they appear on the host's input
# stack either way. On a desktop host, this keeps them out of the local
# session: no seat, no ACL for the logged-in user (uaccess), root only, and
# libinput ignores them. Environments reach them through their own device
# nodes, which this doesn't touch.
#
# - The Xbox 360 pad goes through /dev/uinput with phys "cha/padN".
# - The DualSense and the Steam Controller go through /dev/uhid, and look like
#   the real thing: the vendors' ids on the bus a real one uses. The kernel
#   names each HID device bus:vendor:product.N, and these are every one the
#   streamer can make:
#     0003:054C:0CE6  DualSense, USB
#     0005:28DE:1303  2026 Steam Controller, Bluetooth (what it makes now)
#     0005:28DE:1106  original Steam Controller, Bluetooth
#     0003:28DE:1102  original Steam Controller, USB
#   (The streamer picks one Steam Controller at build time; the rule lists all
#   three so changing that pick needs no rule change.) The host's
#   hid-playstation, hid-steam or hid-generic bind them and make input nodes,
#   and Steam's own udev rules (60-steam-input.rules) and 70-uaccess would
#   hand their hidraw nodes to the person at the desk. What tells ours apart
#   from the real ones is the parent: a uhid device sits under
#   /devices/virtual/misc/uhid, while a controller on the desk is on a real
#   USB or Bluetooth path. (A DualSense or Steam Controller that some other program
#   makes through uhid is treated the same, which is the point: it isn't a
#   controller this machine's user holds.) The rules match both subsystems:
#   "input" for the evdev nodes (gamepad, touchpad, motion sensors) and
#   "hidraw" for the raw one.
#
# - With CHA_STEAM_PAD_TRANSPORT=usbip the Steam Controller is a real USB
#   device the streamer serves through the kernel's vhci_hcd loopback
#   (0003:28DE:1302, usbhid/hid-generic). It enumerates under
#   /devices/platform/vhci_hcd.0, which no controller on the desk does, so the
#   last rule below matches on that parent, as the uhid one does on its own.
#
# Install (root), and again after an update that changes this file:
#   sudo deploy/node/host/install.sh
#
# 72: after 70-uaccess and 71-seat tag the device, before 73-seat-late applies
# the tags.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{phys}=="cha/pad*", TAG-="uaccess", TAG-="seat", ENV{ID_SEAT}="seat-cha", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1", MODE="0600"
SUBSYSTEM=="input|hidraw", DEVPATH=="*/virtual/misc/uhid/*", KERNELS=="0003:054C:0CE6.*|0005:28DE:1303.*|0005:28DE:1106.*|0003:28DE:1102.*", TAG-="uaccess", TAG-="seat", ENV{ID_SEAT}="seat-cha", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1", MODE="0600"
SUBSYSTEM=="input|hidraw", DEVPATH=="*/platform/vhci_hcd.0/*", KERNELS=="0003:28DE:1302.*", TAG-="uaccess", TAG-="seat", ENV{ID_SEAT}="seat-cha", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1", MODE="0600"
